livery-manager: unpack custom-liveries as dictionary entries

custom-liveries is declared `a{sv}`, so its elements are dictionary
entries, not tuples. g_variant_iter_next() validates the format string
against the element type, and "(&sv)" scans as "(sv)", which is not
"{sv}" -- so the call aborts before the first iteration:

  GLib-CRITICAL: the GVariant format string '(&sv)' has a type of
                 '(sv)' but the given value has a type of '{sv}'
  GLib-CRITICAL: g_variant_iter_next: assertion
                 'valid_format_string (format_string, TRUE, value)' failed

The loop body therefore never runs, the custom-liveries hash table stays
empty, and selecting a custom livery falls back to the built-in default
with

  Kgx-WARNING: settings: '<uuid>' is unknown, using default livery

i.e. custom liveries are unreachable in 50.0 by any route: this is the
only consumer of the gsettings key, and kgx_livery_import_from() (the
keyfile path) has no callers yet. Use the dictionary-entry format.

Reported against GNOME Console 50.0.
---
diff --git a/src/kgx-livery-manager.c b/src/kgx-livery-manager.c
--- a/src/kgx-livery-manager.c
+++ b/src/kgx-livery-manager.c
@@ -304,7 +304,7 @@ kgx_livery_manager_set_custom_liveries (KgxLiveryManager *self,
 
   g_hash_table_remove_all (self->custom_liveries);
 
-  while (g_variant_iter_next (iter, "(&sv)", &uuid, &value)) {
+  while (g_variant_iter_next (iter, "{&sv}", &uuid, &value)) {
     g_autoptr (KgxLivery) livery = kgx_livery_deserialise (value);
 
     if (g_strcmp0 (kgx_livery_get_uuid (livery), uuid) != 0) {
